      "code": "if (pct[1] == '2' && pct[2] == '5' && pct[3])",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "note": "This check inspects pct[1], pct[2], and pct[3] to decide whether the '%' is the RFC 6874 '%25' escape, but it never verifies that addr actually contains at least 3 more characters after pct before dereferencing pct[1]..pct[3]; the string could end exactly at or before pct+3, so the safety obligation (remaining length from pct >= 4 bytes before indexing pct[3]) is violated when the literal ends mid-escape (e.g. '%2' or '%25' at the very end of the buffer)."
    },
