      "code": "memmove (pct + 1, pct + 3, strlen (pct + 3) + 1);",
      "role": "sink",
      "note": "strlen(pct + 3) reads past the NUL terminator of addr when pct+3 lies at or beyond the end of the allocated buffer, causing an out-of-bounds heap read (and the subsequent memmove copies based on that bogus length), because the preceding check at line 422 already read pct[3] out of bounds and this line compounds it by using pct+3 as a read pointer with unchecked length."
    }
